ushion.","On multiples it looks expensive against Consumer Cyclical peers: P/E 39.4 vs 19.3, EV/EBITDA 55.4 vs 11.2 and P/FCF 87.4 vs 16.5 (sector median).","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 1.1% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of -1.2% (vs the 8% bar).","The 8 covering analysts target $17.75 on average, 38% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["It runs a 64% gross margin and converts 3% of revenue into free cash flow, or -2% after stock compensation.","Earnings quality is a concern: cash conversion of only -0.89x and high accruals (-19.3% of assets).","Operating margin is running 26pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 4.2% of revenue on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["The balance sheet carries net cash of $151.2M (9% of market cap).","Warning signs: an Altman Z of -1.87 in the distress zone, which caps the rating at HOLD.","The current ratio of 0.86 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 4.7% over 3 years and 18.2% over 5 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 22%).","Margins are expanding (+4.6% trend).","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 27%.","Capex runs only 0.6x depreciation (2.7% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 17, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 161.2% on average."],"own":["Insiders own 7.1%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 95%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (19 sales, net $1.4M sold).","The share count has grown 5.7% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","Short interest is elevated at 16.3% of the float, 6.0 days to cover."],"people":["With about 3,140 employees, each generates about $221K of revenue, 0.6x the Consumer Cyclical median, and productivity has risen 13.9% a year."